      "side": 1,
      "message": "Every comparator must have a hash function, but the spec allows requiring one only \"unless the equality predicate of the comparator is eq?, eqv?, equal?, string\u003d?, or string-ci\u003d?\". `(set (make-comparator #t eq? #f #f) \u0027a \u0027b)` raises \"comparator has no hash function\", and so do eqv?, equal? and string\u003d?. When `(comparator-hashable? c)` is false, make the table from the equality predicate, `(make-hash-table (comparator-equality-predicate c))`, for which (srfi 125) supplies the hash. In `sob-hash` (1308), use the table\u0027s hash function.",
      "revId": "3238d22f6af70e356c32dad7fc3ac652b3a7627b",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
