      "writtenOn": "2026-11-19T21:24:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Performance: `sob-decrement!` leaves a 0 count and `sob-cleanup!` then scans the whole table, so each `set-delete!`, `bag-decrement!` and `set-search!` remove or update is O(n). Deleting all elements one at a time is quadratic. On the debug CLI, 250 / 500 / 1000 elements take 1.4 / 4.3 / 12.1 s, while adjoining them takes 0.05 / 0.10 / 0.14 s. The cleanup pass was there because deleting while iterating was unsafe, and iteration now runs over a snapshot. Delete the entry here when the count reaches ≤ 0, which also fixes the `update` bug at 484.",
      "revId": "3238d22f6af70e356c32dad7fc3ac652b3a7627b",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "634aec23_344d2211",
        "filename": "crates/vali-compiler/lib/srfi/113.sld",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 484,
