        "id": 1040172
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-19T21:24:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`set-search!` with `update` to an element the comparator finds equal removes it. The decrement takes the entry to 0, `sob-increment!` (302) finds the entry and, for a set, leaves it, and cleanup deletes it. With a string-ci comparator:\n\n```scheme\n(set-search! (set ci \"abc\" \"def\") \"ABC\" (lambda (ins ign) (ins \u0027new)) (lambda (x upd rem) (upd \"ABC\" \u0027done)))\n```\n\nThis leaves size 1, and `set-member` of \"abc\" is `absent`. Expected: size 2, holding \"ABC\". Removing an entry as soon as its count reaches 0 (see the comment at 311) fixes this too.",
      "revId": "3238d22f6af70e356c32dad7fc3ac652b3a7627b",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
