      "message": "Nit: with one argument, `set-union`, `set-intersection` (1030), `set-difference` (1076) and `bag-sum` (1122) return the argument itself. The spec says newly allocated, and `(set-adjoin! (set-union s) 99)` then changes `s`. Return `(sob-copy sob1)`.",
