      "writtenOn": "2026-11-19T21:24:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`set-xor!` and `bag-xor!` (called with `result` \u003d `sob1`, 1210 and 1216) lose the elements only the second argument has. Pass 1 adds sob2-only keys to sob1. Pass 2 then iterates sob1, finds them in both, writes |v−v| \u003d 0, and cleanup removes them.\n\n- `(set-\u003elist (set-xor! (set c 1 2) (set c 2 3)))` gives `(1)`, expected `(1 3)`. The pure `set-xor` gets it right.\n- `(set-xor! (set c) (set c 5))` gives `()`.\n\nThe sample has the same bug, and the regression test only xors equal sets. Snapshot both before writing, or add sob2\u0027s keys absent from sob1 after scanning sob1. Test presence, not count.",
      "revId": "3238d22f6af70e356c32dad7fc3ac652b3a7627b",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
