      "lineNbr": 762,
      "author": {
        "id": 1040172
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-19T21:24:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Two problems with this hash.\n\n**It doesn\u0027t terminate on circular data.** It hashes every value with the value comparator\u0027s hash, which for `mapping-comparator` is `default-hash`, with a fresh budget each call. Since `mapping-comparator` is registered (776), `default-hash` recurses into mappings without end:\n\n```scheme\n(define v (vector #f)) (define m (mapping c 1 v)) (vector-set! v 0 m) (default-hash v)\n```\n\nThis was still running after 30 s. Left longer it dies with a fatal \"stack overflow\", which `guard` can\u0027t catch. A plain circular vector hashes at once, as 128.sld promises. `make-hashmap-comparator` (hash.sld:451) has the same shape.\n\n**It claims a hash it can\u0027t compute.** It is offered whenever the value comparator is hashable (771), but it also needs the key comparator\u0027s hash. So `(comparator-hashable? mapping-comparator)` is #t, yet with `m \u003d (mapping (make-comparator real? \u003d \u003c #f) 1 \u0027a 2 \u0027b)`, `(comparator-hash mapping-comparator m)` raises \"comparator has no hash function\". So does `default-hash` of anything holding such a mapping.\n\nFix for both: hash the size and the key hashes of at most a few keys, leaving values out. Equal mappings have equal keys, so that stays consistent with `mapping\u003d?`. Use only the size when the key comparator can\u0027t hash.",
      "revId": "3238d22f6af70e356c32dad7fc3ac652b3a7627b",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
